NAVONLINE_DRY_RUN = Dry-run (trial operation)
NAVONLINE_DRY_RUN_Help = When on, the XML is built and validated (XSD + pzs) and stored with a DRYRUN_ prefix, but nothing is sent and NAV is not called at all (no credentials needed). Rows stay pending and are sent normally once dry-run is switched off.
NAVONLINE_SEND_ON_VALIDATE = Send immediately on validation
NAVONLINE_SEND_ON_VALIDATE_Help = When on, the invoice is sent right after its validation is committed (at the end of the same request) instead of waiting for the 5-minute scheduled run. If sending fails (e.g. NAV outage) the invoice stays queued and the scheduled run retries it. Sending never blocks the validation.
NavOnlineAlertSection = E-mail alerts
NAVONLINE_ALERT_EMAIL = Alert e-mail addresses
NAVONLINE_ALERT_EMAIL_Help = Comma separated. A summary e-mail is sent about invoices in error, NAV ABORTED results, rejected/aborted technical annulments, invoices waiting too long and configuration errors. At most every 24 h per invoice, every 6 h for configuration errors.
NAVONLINE_ALERT_STALE_HOURS = Waiting alert (hours)
NAVONLINE_ALERT_STALE_HOURS_Help = Alert about invoices not sent, without a final result or with an unapproved annulment after this many hours (default: 12).
